    {
      "id": "a157c96fca8d4493776b20e2896957c34f9ae82b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2510719389,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> No default ports were specified for some reason.\n\nThe reason being that the ports are not IANA registered, which is easy to do.\n\nThe dissector has no heuristics and will never reject a packet on those ports. Since the ports are not IANA registered to the protocol (and one ports is registered to a different protocol), it's inappropriate to default it to that port; for the average user's capture it's more likely *not* to be HSFZ than to be it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-05-17T16:19:33.919Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-05-17T16:19:33.919Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 384133952,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 19878,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a30a204688510c7c4e69de3adb16fc00805c20d1",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2510720367,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hummm, now I know... Thanks!\n\nWould it make sense to add heuristics to verify that the packets are actually from that particular protocol?\n\nWould it make sense to register the protocol to that port but letting the other protocol take preference over HSFZ?\n\nPlease, let me know if there is something that can be done to improve this.\n\nThanks for the info! :D",
          "author": {
            "id": 2445059,
            "username": "antoniovazquezblanco",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Antonio Vázquez Blanco",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3003c2b03cbc9f8b4f0fb99281e9d1ede120aac36545e6664cec362f0af5c3af?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/antoniovazquezblanco"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-05-17T16:25:04.016Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-05-17T16:25:04.016Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 384133952,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 19878,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "d3c6e983923931bf59323243966b987f10f69549",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2510727239,
          "type": null,
          "body": "It might be possible for the UDP case, but it's unfortunately fairly difficult to have something that can be segmented over multiple TCP segments dissected heuristically.\n\nIf someone can write a heuristic dissector for the protocol, that would be good. I haven't looked at the protocol too closely to see how feasible that is. Otherwise, unfortunately it's difficult to set the port as default for all Wireshark users (as opposed to letting people configure it via Decode As for their own profile.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-05-17T17:04:09.747Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-05-17T17:04:09.747Z",
